            "review_text": "Thomas R\n16 contributions\n0\nAmazing charcuterie!\nNov 2019\nThis tiny restaurant is almost invisible as you stroll down Ly Quoc Su Street. The quality of the food, however, makes it well worth the effort. The window display shows off the excellent charcuterie, including home-made patés and terrines, home made salamis and fresh baked baguettes. Sandwiches can be eaten in the restaurant or taken out, and the freshly cooked main courses make a second visit well worth your while.\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten November 19, 2019",
