            "review_title": "Review at Nguyen Sinh",
            "review_text": "oiboy\nMontreal, Canada166 contributions\n0\nSkip the Bahn Mi. Get a Chacuterie Plate with Bread\nAug 2019 • Solo\nAmazing Pate. I'm still dreaming about it. This is not your typical bahn mi shop with pickled veggies and chua la. This place has artisanal meat made in house along with the best pate I've had in Vietnam. In fact it's up there with some of the best I've had in France at certain Michelin star places. I would suggest getting a Chacuterie plate along with a couple of bread loaves to try it. You will likely spend about 80-100k here but the quality of the food really exceeds the price. There was a steady stream of locals who stopped in to buy the pate they sell by the tub full. This place is not really a tourist trap (like the pho place across the street) and has been here for many many years. Trust me its worth the trip!\nRead more\nWritten August 10, 2019",
            "rating": 5.0,
