            "review_text": "Chicky-Athens\nBoston, Massachusetts99 contributions\n0\nOne of the best banh mi in Vietnam: Great Steak!\nFeb 2018 • Solo\nI loved this dingy little place. A Vietnamese-French cafe. I stopped to test a banh mi \"sub\" after I saw the meat in the window. They use the old fashioned style \"cold-cut\" meats that every banh mi seller was using when I fist visited Vietnam in 1994. It's very rare nowadays as other sellers use the cheaper processed meat. The banh mi was delicious and I made several sorties over several weeks. They also offer a few sizes, which is also rare in my experience. Yes, the larger banh mi are more expensive than the cart on the street, but the quality of meat and pate are much higher, as well. \n\nI also treated myself to a steak a couple of times after seeing that's what the locals were there for. Also a good value. \n\nThis is not shiny and beautiful restaurant. It does, however, have one of the best authentic banh mi in Vietnam.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nWritten April 11, 2018",
